# Project S — always-on agent rules

## Notebook safety (hard)

- Work only on `Jigar_Q&A_Branch_Baseline_COPY.ipynb`. Never edit the original or the backup.
- Never run any notebook cell. Never use Run all. Do not run Python that imports torch, transformers or A_predict. Editing scripts that only read and write `.ipynb` JSON are allowed.
- Edit the notebook with a small Python script that changes only the listed cells. Do not rewrite the whole notebook. Do not touch outputs or execution_count.
- Never edit or delete Blocks 12, 17, 22, 26, 42 or the old duplicate helper cells.
- Before any edit, show the plan and wait for "go". After editing, check against the 162-cell reference: valid JSON, same untouched cells, same outputs and execution counts.
- No hosted LLM or API in the deployed scorer (rule L8). Local open-weights models are fine.
- New blocks start at Block 61. Files in `reports_v2/` start with `A_`. Never overwrite `question_bank_v1.csv`.
- Test numbers are exploratory. Dev numbers are optimistic. If a number is not in the notebook, write "not in notebook". Never invent one.

## How to treat this project

- Status labels matter: proposed work is never presented as a completed result.
- Say "the paper suggests X, and we will test it" unless it was measured on our data.
- Q&A numbers in section 5A were measured on public English data (SciEntsBank and Beetle), not NNCES or CBSE.
- Evidence labels: (E) paper finding; (P) our proposal; (I) inference; (doc) copied and not re-checked; (NV) not verified; (M) measured on dev (optimistic).

## Project in one line

ML-based multimodal system: children's oral-reading and comprehension scored separately, then a multidimensional skill profile with uncertainty and no overall score.

## What is built vs not (as of 31 Oct 2026)

- Askar baseline stays: file list, audio check, acoustic features, wav2vec2 last-layer embeddings, age experiment 42.01% ± 4.61%. Pitch audit still required (implausible ~47–52 Hz).
- Q&A scorer v2, review rule, and Gradio demo are built and measured on public data. Reading-branch components remain pending (reference text, human ratings, miscues).
- Deployed scorer: average of DistilRoBERTa, SBERT-LR, NLI-LR. No LLM, no hosted API.
- Review: calibrated confidence below 0.64. ECE 0.017. 85% accuracy at 30% coverage is not met.
- Unseen-question QWK on dev: 0.317 (0.199 to 0.412), 27 questions, below the 0.55–0.60 plan.
- Demo/notebook parity PASS on 15 of 15 (largest confidence difference 0.0005). Consistency, not independent replication.
- Never use Run all: a 30 Oct 2026 full run rewrote 18 files meant to be frozen.

## Locked decisions (do not reopen)

- L1: `non_domain` stays score 0 with a separate needs-review flag.
- L2: v1 files frozen; new results go to `_v2` files.
- L3: select on dev only; further test results are exploratory.
- L4: English only; synthetic answers train-only if ever used.
- L5: QWK only on ordered 3-level labels; accuracy and macro-F1 on official 5 labels.
- L6: CBSE is an extension; public data proves the pipeline.
- L7: rubric-prompted LLM is a small-sample side result, not the final scorer.
- L8: scorer is completely ML/DL; no external API or hosted LLM.

